---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// The deepest honesty claim on the page: a perfectly-sourced answer refused by
// the first hard check, before the backing check runs. Mechanism per
// INTELLIGENCE.md §3. biological_age_estimate is a real corpus note id.
---

<Section id="guardrail" tone="sunk" labelledby="guardrail-h">
  <p class="eyebrow rise">Even a good answer can be refused</p>
  <h2 id="guardrail-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    A perfect source doesn’t save an answer it shouldn’t give.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    Most “grounded” apps stop at one question: does every claim have a source? Ours asks a harder one
    first — is this something we should be telling you at all?
  </p>

  <figure
    class="surface surface-lift rise mt-10 max-w-3xl p-6 sm:p-8"
    aria-label="Rendered example: a validly sourced life-expectancy projection being refused"
  >
    <figcaption class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
        Hard check 1 &middot; example
      </span>
      <span class="chip chip-warn chip-dot">refused</span>
    </figcaption>

    <div class="turn turn-user">
      <span class="turn-who">You asked</span>
      <p class="turn-body">&ldquo;My biological age is 34 — how many years do I have left?&rdquo;</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who">The model drafted this — and it was correctly sourced</span>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed">
        <span class="blocked"
          >“Based on your biological age of 34, your modelled remaining life expectancy is about 48
          years</span
        ><span class="cite blocked">&nbsp;[biological_age_estimate]</span><span class="blocked"
          >.”</span
        >
      </p>
      <p class="mono mt-2 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        The note is real and the wording is fair. The backing check would have passed it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="verdict mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who" style="color:var(--c-warn)">Why it was refused</span>
      <p class="text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">
        This is a personal life-expectancy projection — refused no matter how good the source is, and
        caught <em>before</em> the backing check ever runs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="hairline my-6" />

    <div class="turn turn-coach">
      <span class="turn-who">What you get instead</span>
      <div class="turn-body">
        <p>
          Your biological-age estimate is a motivating fitness trend — driven mostly by your fitness,
          sleep, and how regular your nights are <span class="cite">[biological_age_estimate]</span>
          — not a countdown clock. I won’t project your remaining years; that’s not something this
          number can honestly tell you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>

  <p class="mono rise mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
    No competitor prints this, because no competitor can. It’s the difference between a source-checker
    and a product with a line it won’t cross.
  </p>
</Section>
